{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3n91dz1C43gWiEiY15K","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added `scripts/export_invoices.py` and committed it along with its output, `out/invoices.csv` (8 of the 12 invoices).\n\n**Segment C customers are left out.** The customers export drops segment C, and the commit that added that filter explains why: those customers declined partner sharing, and that covers every record we hold on them, not just the customers table. Invoices have no segment column, so the new script looks up each invoice's customer in `tables/customers.csv` and drops any that belong to segment C. That removed invoices 9002 and 9008 (customer 103, Cedar Works) and 9005 and 9011 (customer 105, Elm Trading). I read through the output file and none of those four are in it.\n\nThe commit message starts `export_invoices:` like the earlier customers export commit, since there's no data month for this one. It touched nothing under `data/`, so `check.sh` didn't apply. As you asked, I left January alone and it's still only in `inbox/`.\n\nOne command was blocked by the permission system: an inline Python check of the output. I checked the same thing by reading the output file instead.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":346,"cache_read_input_tokens":22174,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":346,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-74>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T00:37:32.427Z","request_id":"gen-1794703047-c190t3umvLbsCnXqAqDX"}
